## 5 · NEC-SE-GC 2015 (official)

#: NEC-15 **gives no method** to compute piles with the CPT: it only uses it for soil parameters (§6.3.1, p. 42). The sum of shaft and base of §8.2 (p. 50) and the **FS = 3.0 of Table 6** (p. 42) with dead + normal live load are taken; applying it to the whole pile is our criterion. In GEO5: "Safety factors (ASD)" setting, SF_{b} = 3.0, which works **without ξ** (checked today in GEO5, capture "nec/02_asd_bearing_capacity": F_{r,d} = 2810.00 kN, F_{s,d} = 1800.00 kN, FS = 1.56 < 3.00, NOT SATISFACTORY).
FS_req = 3.0 'Table 6, dead + normal live load
F_rd = n_p·R_ci 'resistance of the group with ASD, without ξ [kN]
FS_g = F_rd/F_sd 'factor of safety of the group
Q_adm = F_rd/FS_req 'allowable load of the group by NEC-15 [kN]
Q_adm_t = Q_adm/9.80665 'allowable load of the group [tonf]
F_s_t = n_p·F_s1/9.80665 'service load of the group [tonf]
#hide
r_fs = round(FS_g, 2)
r_qa = round(Q_adm_t, 1)
r_ft = round(F_s_t, 1)
r_fss = round(F_rd/(n_p·F_s1), 2)
#show
#: FS = @{r_fs} < 3.0: **does not comply with NEC-15**. Even with the service load (@{r_ft} tonf against @{r_qa} tonf allowable) the FS is @{r_fss}. With clays of q_{c} ≈ 0.5 MPa, 15 m of pile is not enough: they must be lengthened or more piles added.
#: **2023 draft (unofficial):** FS from 2.0 to 3.0 depending on control, and LRFD for driven piles with CPT φ = 0.50 in compression (Table 6.5); GEO5 Pile CPT has no LRFD.

